<!--
    An even ARM function symbol starts A32 code (GH-842).

    The XML wrapper only provides the harness architecture. Every pass clears
    it and loads one of the synthetic ARM32 ELFs from
    `arm_funcmode_le32.py`: an A32 `entry` at 0x2000000 that runs
    `blx 0x2000040` and `bl 0x2000080`, a Thumb `thumb_helper` symbol at
    0x2000041 (`movs r0,#7; bx lr`) and an A32 `arm_helper` symbol at
    0x2000080 (`add r0,r0,#1; bx lr`).

    Before the pass, on GH-842's image (no mapping symbols) the Thumb mode of
    `thumb_helper` (its symbol, and the `blx`) reached `arm_helper`, which
    decoded as Thumb and ran off the image. Pass 1 sets A32 at the even
    `arm_helper` symbol: `return a0 + 1`.

    Pass 2 uses the image whose `blx` is a `nop`, so only the odd
    `thumb_helper` symbol carries Thumb: `arm_helper` is A32 there too.

    Pass 3 uses GH-842's image with `$a`/`$t`/`$a` mapping symbols. The pass
    paints nothing there, and `arm_helper` decodes as A32.

    The A32 paint covers a function symbol's size, cut at the next function
    symbol, and the Thumb mode resumes past it. A size-0 symbol states no
    extent and is skipped: pass 4 uses the image whose `arm_helper` has size
    0, and it still decodes as Thumb.

    Pass 5 uses `arm_static_thumb_so_o2_le32`, a gcc -O2 armel shared
    object (`.dynsym` only) whose A32 `arm_export` follows the Thumb
    `thumb_first`: it is the A32 loop `s += i ^ 0x33`.

    Pass 6 uses `arm_funcmode_helper_o2_le32.so` (clang -O2, linked with
    lld, stripped): the A32 export `a_func` calls an unsymbolized A32 static
    helper at 0x1020c with `bl`. The A32 extent grows over a direct A32
    branch target before the next function symbol, so the helper is not
    handed back to Thumb where the extent ends.

    Passes 7 to 9 bound that growth. A run ends at a call to a function that
    never returns (`abort`, `__stack_chk_fail`) and adds nothing if it meets
    no stop before the next function symbol, and words a PC-relative `ldr`
    loads are data: in `arm_funcmode_noreturn_le32.so` (clang -O2, the A32
    helper calls `abort`) and `arm_funcmode_stackprot_le32.so` (clang -O2
    -fstack-protector-all) the unsymbolized Thumb `t_help` behind the A32
    helper, and in `arm_funcmode_pool_le32` the Thumb `t_s` behind an A32
    function whose literal pool holds a word shaped like a `b`, keep Thumb.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
